Q: How can I restrict a method to only classes implementing a specific interface in Java? A: <blockquote>
<p>What would be the idiomatic Java design for enforcing this restriction?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't know about idiomatic, but the way I would do this is to change the method signature from <code>public void heal(int amount)</code> to <code>public void receiveHealing(Healer source)</code>.</p>
<p>Instead of accepting an integer, forcing the method to require a <code>Healer</code> object uses Java's type system to guarantee that a heal is impossible unless an actual <code>Healer</code> is present to initiate it.</p>
<p>This is an example I ran on my side:</p>
<pre><code>abstract class GameCharacter {
    protected int health = 50;

    public void receiveHealing(Healer source) {
        this.health += source.getHealingPower();
        System.out.println(this.getClass().getSimpleName() + &quot; healed! Health: &quot; + this.health);
    }
}

class Warrior extends GameCharacter {
    // Warrior cannot heal anyone.
}

class Healer extends GameCharacter {
    private int healingPower = 20;

    public int getHealingPower() { // This is the public property
        return healingPower;
    }

    public void healTarget(GameCharacter target) { // This is where the healing actually happens
        target.receiveHealing(this);
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Warrior warrior = new Warrior();
        Healer healer = new Healer();

        healer.healTarget(warrior);
        healer.healTarget(healer);

        // For Testing
        // warrior.receiveHealing(20); 
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Inside <code>GameCharacter.receiveHealing()</code>, the code doesn't just know the number in some magical way. Instead, it extracts it from the Healer object that was passed in, using this line: <code>this.health += source.getHealingPower();</code></p>

Q: How to call any model function from common helper in codeigniter A: <p>In constructor of common helper:</p>

<pre><code>public function __construct() {
    // Assign the CodeIgniter super-object
    $this-&gt;CI = &amp; get_instance();
}

//Now for loading a model
public function addAudit($id_user,$description){
    $this-&gt;CI-&gt;load-&gt;model('your_model_name');
    $response_audit =  $this-&gt;CI-&gt;your_model_name-&gt;addAudit($id_user,$description);
            if($response_audit){
                log_message('debug',' Product --addAudit :: Response received from model'); 
                }else{
                log_message('debug',' Product --addAudit :: Response didnot received from model'); 
            }
}
</code></pre>

Q: Calling a model in a Helper file using codeigniter A: <p>Check this post:</p>

<pre><code>function my_helper()
{
    // Get a reference to the controller object
    //$CI = get_instance();
    // use this below
    $CI = &amp;get_instance();

    // You may need to load the model if it hasn't been pre-loaded
    $CI-&gt;load-&gt;model('my_model');

    // Call a function of the model
    $CI-&gt;my_model-&gt;do_something();
}
</code></pre>

